  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Input**\n\nI\'m currently digesting the user\'s request. I understand they want an app with specific screen designs, and they\'ve provided image examples. I\'m focusing on hotlinking images from HTML as a viable design approach. I\'m starting to visualize the app\'s structure based on the provided images.\n\n\n**Integrating New Requirements**\n\nI\'ve got a clearer picture of the app\'s components, including Fisiopatolog\303\255a, Curvas Kraft, and the calculator screen. The latest development includes incorporating new requirements, like a game-like structure with levels and a modern color scheme, which demands a more interactive user experience. These new details alter the design approach considerably. I need to make sure the app feels engaging!\n\n\n**Clarifying the Ambiguity**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a crucial ambiguity. The instructions are potentially conflicting. I\'m carefully analyzing whether the gamified \"levels of complexity\" relate to a broader clinical challenge simulator *in addition* to, or *instead* of, the core clinical decision support platform \"EndoMetabolic Rx.\" I need to determine if it\'s the full platform *plus* a game, or if the gamification *is* the application\'s primary focus. This impacts the entire scope.\n\n\n**Reconciling Different Visions**\n\nI\'m now wrestling with the conflicting requirements. The initial design request is for a standard CDSS app based on specific screens. However, I now have a new set of instructions, \"la app debe usar colores modernos, debe ser un juego llamativo, inicialmente vamos a realizar 10 niveles , lo cuales se iran incrementa el nivel de complejidad.\" My current thinking is to include *both*: the complete CDSS app as originally designed *and* a separate, engaging gamified \"Clinical Simulator\" mode with 10 increasing levels. I\'m focusing on elegantly integrating these two distinct components.\n\n\n"
