  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the User\'s Request**\n\nI\'m starting to break down the user\'s request. It seems they want an app with specific screen designs, potentially pulling images directly from HTML. I\'m focusing on the implied need for modern color palettes, too. Now I am trying to determine what a good strategy is for this app, and to think about the best approach.\n\n\n**Defining the Application\'s Scope**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the application\'s core functionality. The initial focus will be on 10 levels of increasing complexity, as suggested. I\'m starting with the provided HTML and screenshots. I see EndoMetabolic Rx as the base, and have a clear outline of screens. Now, I\'m analyzing the 4 specific screens (Fisiopatolog\303\255a y ATM, Calculadora de \303\215ndices Subrogados, etc.) and the provided HTML templates and design system tokens.\n\n\n**Elaborating Feature Requirements**\n\nI\'m now detailing the user\'s requirements for the app\'s outputs. I\'m focusing on the left panel inputs (biological sex, glucose, insulin, etc.) and considering the dynamic recalculation and reset buttons, alongside the metabolic friction accumulator bar. I\'m also planning the eight biomarker cards: HOMA-IR, QUICKI, and others. Each will display dynamic sparklines, cutoffs, interpretations, and risk badges. Furthermore, I\'m thinking about the CDSS intervention.\n\n\n**Defining CDSS Functionality**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the CDSS functionality and its integration within the app. I\'m focusing on the Metabolic Risk Stratum timeline, from Estrato 0 to 3, and the SHAP Risk Predictors (XGBoost Fenotipador). I have planned the attribution bars, directives for immediate action, biochemical countermeasures, and safety guidelines. I\'m also planning the cellular research visual panels. I\'m also analyzing the clinical plan commit bar. Furthermore, I\'ve started organizing the \"Matriz Terap\303\251utica\" and \"Monitoreo y FHIR\" tabs, which will be added to navigation.\n\n\n"
