  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Application Requirements**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the application\'s required screens and features to ensure a state-of-the-art design. Key elements include a header with the logo, title (\"EndoMetabolic Rx\"), and a subtitle (\"SISTEMA DE SOPORTE PARA DECISIONES CL\303\215NICAS EN MEDICINA FUNCIONAL\"). There will also be a clinical toggle option: \"Modo\".\n\n\n**Defining Gamified Challenge Mode**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the \"Desaf\303\255o Cl\303\255nico\" (Clinical Challenge) mode. This 10-level gamified section will be the core of the experience, as requested. I\'ve broken down patient info into a persistent quick bar, including Eleanor Vance\'s data. Navigation tabs will direct users to various features like Kraft curves, and FHIR integration for monitoring. I\'m focusing on the integration of risk stratification (Strata 2) and vital parameters into a persistent sidebar for easy access. Active interventions are also displayed.\n\n\n**Detailing Screen Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the specific functionality of Screen 1: \"Fisiopatolog\303\255a y ATM\". I\'m prioritizing the patient banner with Eleanor Vance\'s data and incorporating interactive elements like the FHIR tree and Etiological Map regeneration. I\'m also fleshing out the Longitudinal Metabolic Progression with key epochs and ensuring all expandable elements within the Fisiopatolog\303\255a ATM framework contain rich, detailed biological information. I\'m also planning the design of the 7 Nodes of the Functional Medicine Matrix.\n\n\n**Elaborating Metabolic Matrix**\n\nI\'m now detailing the functional medicine matrix nodes and synthesizing the CDSS card with a sequential 3-step plan, with integration of modal features. I\'m focusing on \"Integridad Estructural\" and also building an \"Inspector Modal\" for in-depth examination, plus adding patient protocols. Further work is being done on the diagnostic report modal, which includes syntax highlighting and JSON export, and finally, toast notifications.\n\n**Developing Index Calculator**\n\nI\'m moving onto screen 2, \"Calculadora de \303\215ndices Subrogados,\" matching image 7. I\'m concentrating on the live editable input panel now. I will be working on elements like biological sex, and fasting glucose and insulin levels. Also triglycerides, HDL cholesterol, BMI, and waist circumference. I\'m focusing on defining this panel now.\n\n\n**Designing Index Calculator Features**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Recalcular \303\215ndices\" button and \"Restablecer Valores\" functionality. I\'m prioritizing the implementation of a live metabolic friction gauge, aiming for real-time visualization. I\'m also now structuring 8 dynamic clinical cards, including HOMA-IR, QUICKI, and others, each with a dynamic SVG sparkline and risk classification. Furthermore, all calculations will be responsive and update instantly with input changes, and I\'m adding an action drawer for CDSS interventions and reporting.\n\n\n**Constructing Kraft Curve Detail**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the detailed design of the high-fidelity Kraft curve visualization for the Metabolic Patterns analysis. I am planning on adding a dual-axis interactive SVG chart with smooth morphing curves. The left axis will display glucose (mg/dL) with threshold guidelines, and the right axis will show insulin (\302\265IU/mL) with hyperinsulinemic toxicity hazard hatching. There will also be a dynamic shaded Area Under the Curve (AUC) and interactive nodes for time points with tooltip values. I plan to incorporate a 5-point data breakdown row and a Pancreatic Kinetics analysis card. Finally, there will be a diagnostic verdict box that states \"Patr\303\263n Kraft.\"\n\n\n**Defining Risk Stratification**\n\nI\'m now focusing on Screen 4, \"CDSS y Estratificaci\303\263n,\" and the four-stage interactive timeline for metabolic risk strata. I\'m building out the SHAP Risk Attribution Engine, visualizing protective and aggravating vectors using a force plot. The objective is to define the left and right columns. I also have the Kraft patterns reference matrix. I am looking at clinical levers and biomarkers.\n\n\n\n**Formulating Clinical Protocols**\n\nI\'m now detailing actionable treatments for Screen 5, \"Matriz Terap\303\251utica.\" I\'m prioritizing the 5R Gut Restoration Protocol and targeted nutraceutical schedules, including chrononutrition and Zone 2 exercise tracking. I\'m also adding a drug-nutrient interaction checker and clinical contraindication guard. Furthermore, I\'ve defined Immediate Action Levers, Biochemical Countermeasures, and Safety Directives. I\'m building a research and biopsy visual grid for microscopy and ultrasounds. Finally, I will be working on a FHIR Clinical Protocol Execution Bar.\n\n\n**Designing Telemetry & Challenge**\n\nI\'m now detailing Screen 6, \"Monitoreo y FHIR,\" with live glucose telemetry simulation, TIR data, and a FHIR R4 JSON interactive viewer. Simultaneously, I\'m working on Screen 7, the 10-level Clinical Challenge, starting with \"Nivel 1: Fricci\303\263n Subcl\303\255nica Temprana.\" I\'m also planning the levels, including \"Nivel 2: Disfunci\303\263n de Fase Cef\303\241lica\" and up to \"Nivel 4: Resistencia Establecida del Receptor.\"\n\n\n**Developing Clinical Challenge Levels**\n\nI\'m now detailing the remaining levels of the Clinical Challenge. I\'ve broken down each level by metabolic phase and associated issues, such as myocellular toxicity and neuro-incretin imbalance. I\'m also planning the user interface, which will have a vibrant visual theme with neon accents and glowing bio elements, a level selector, and real patient lab data and Kraft charts. Furthermore, I\'ve outlined the mechanics and gamification: star ratings, live clinical case triage, and challenge questions per level.\n\n\n**Organizing Codebase Elements**\n\nI\'m now focused on organizing the codebase for a clean architecture. I\'m establishing comprehensive TypeScript interfaces for key data structures. This includes types for patients, lab biomarkers, surrogate calculations, Kraft patterns, ATM matrix, CDSS recommendations, FHIR resources, and the 10 game levels. I\'m also creating specific files for patient data (like Eleanor Vance) and game level data, including medical cases and questions. Finally, I am including utils for metabolic calculators.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_499571"
      name: "create_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Content\":\"export type ScreenTab =\\n  | \'pathophysiology-atm\'\\n  | \'surrogate-indices\'\\n  | \'kraft-ogtt-curves\'\\n  | \'cdss-stratification\'\\n  | \'therapeutics-matrix\'\\n  | \'monitoring-fhir\'\\n  | \'clinical-game\';\\n\\nexport type KraftPatternId =\\n  | \'pattern-1\'\\n  | \'pattern-2\'\\n  | \'pattern-3a\'\\n  | \'pattern-3b\'\\n  | \'pattern-4\'\\n  | \'pattern-5\';\\n\\nexport interface PatientLabs {\\n  glucoseFasting: number; // mg/dL\\n  insulinFasting: number; // uIU/mL\\n  triglycerides: number; // mg/dL\\n  hdl: number; // mg/dL\\n  bmi: number; // kg/m\302\262\\n  waistCm: number; // cm\\n  ggt: number; // U/L\\n  sex: \'female\' | \'male\';\\n}\\n\\nexport interface SurrogateResults {\\n  homaIr: number;\\n  quicki: number;\\n  tyg: number;\\n  tygBmi: number;\\n  metsIr: number;\\n  lap: number;\\n  vai: number;\\n  fli: number;\\n  frictionPercent: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface KraftDataPoint {\\n  timeMin: number;\\n  label: string;\\n  glucose: number;\\n  insulin: number;\\n  status: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface KraftPatternInfo {\\n  id: KraftPatternId;\\n  name: string;\\n  badge: string;\\n  badgeType: \'optimal\' | \'warning\' | \'critical\';\\n  description: string;\\n  glucosePoints: number[];\\n  insulinPoints: number[];\\n  insulinPath: string;\\n  insulinArea: string;\\n  glucosePath: string;\\n  matsuda: number;\\n  aucInsulin: number;\\n  clearanceRatio: number;\\n  phase1Status: string;\\n  phase2Status: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface AtmItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  title: string;\\n  badge?: string;\\n  badgeClass?: string;\\n  icon?: string;\\n  description: string;\\n  extraDetails?: { label: string; value: string; color?: string }[];\\n}\\n\\nexport interface MatrixNodeDetail {\\n  id: string;\\n  nodeNumber: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  subtitle: string;\\n  statusText: string;\\n  statusType: \'optimal\' | \'friction\' | \'severe\';\\n  icon: string;\\n  accentColor: string;\\n  parameters: {\\n    label: string;\\n    value: string;\\n    note?: string;\\n    barPercent?: number;\\n    colorClass?: string;\\n  }[];\\n  treatmentTag: string;\\n  treatmentIcon: string;\\n  deepDescription: string;\\n  protocol: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface GameLevel {\\n  id: number;\\n  levelNumber: number;\\n  title: string;\\n  subtitle: string;\\n  difficulty: \'Principiante\' | \'Intermedio\' | \'Avanzado\' | \'Experto\' | \'Maestro Cl\303\255nico\';\\n  stratumTarget: \'Estrato 0\' | \'Estrato 1\' | \'Estrato 2\' | \'Estrato 3\';\\n  patient: {\\n    name: string;\\n    age: number;\\n    sex: \'F\' | \'M\';\\n    occupation: string;\\n    symptoms: string;\\n  };\\n  labs: PatientLabs;\\n  kraftPattern: KraftPatternId;\\n  primaryAtmMediator: string;\\n  primaryNode: string;\\n  questions: {\\n    id: string;\\n    prompt: string;\\n    options: {\\n      text: string;\\n      correct: boolean;\\n      explanation: string;\\n    }[];\\n  }[];\\n}\\n\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/types.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating types.ts\", \"toolSummary\":\"Create types for clinical decision support\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
